  "summary": "New work links specific adaptors, lipid regulators and condensates to organelle turnover across ER, mitochondria, peroxisomes, lysosomes and endosomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is stress-responsive organelle remodeling, mostly via selective autophagy and its regulators, though the items span different compartments. Preprints describe Contact-phagy, in which SIGMAR1-CCPG1 turns over ER-mitochondria contact-site subdomains, and Mdm1, an ER-vacuole tether that balances phospholipid and neutral lipid metabolism to allow autophagosome completion in yeast. Another preprint ties NRF2 activation and autophagy to clearance of lipofuscin-like granules in RPE cells. Published work links iron deficiency to pexophagy through GABARAP-FLCN/FNIP1 activation of TFEB and TFE3, shows processing bodies collaborating with stress granules after lysosomal damage, and places RAB11-RAB30 on endosomes using a phosphoinositide switch. New here are the specific adaptors, tethers and condensates assigned to each stress context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
